WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.530
"The Batman" brings the Riddler to life in
a brutal new way, courtesy of actor Paul Dano,

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.810
who gives the villain a sinister edge.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.000
Which brutal act is the worst of the worst?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.269
Caution: spoilers ahead.

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:17.805
"What is the price for your blind eye?"

00:00:17.805 --> 00:00:21.960
The Riddler begins as Edward Nashton, a former
resident of an orphanage once run by Thomas

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.560
and Martha Wayne, Bruce Wayne's parents.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.800
When Edward and Bruce were children, Thomas
announced his run for mayor of Gotham City.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.550
But he and Martha were killed shortly afterward,
leaving his promises of change unfulfilled.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.050
In the final act of the film, the Riddler
has been captured and incarcerated in Arkham

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:43.710
State Hospital, but has left clues indicating
he has one final act of mayhem planned.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.329
Batman interrogates him and learns that Edward
has held a grudge against him since he was

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:48.359
a child.

00:00:48.359 --> 00:00:52.510
When Thomas and Martha Wayne were murdered,
the public's attention was focused entirely

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.089
on young Bruce.

00:00:54.089 --> 00:00:58.530
This left the orphanage forgotten, whose terrible
living conditions Edward describes to Batman

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.170
in painful detail.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.499
While Edward can't be entirely blamed for
feeling jealous of someone who lived in a

00:01:03.499 --> 00:01:08.049
mansion while he suffered in a rundown orphanage,
that's no excuse for taking things out on

00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:10.280
an entire city.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.799
As part of his plan to bring down Gotham City's
elite and reveal their darkest secrets, the

00:01:14.799 --> 00:01:18.920
Riddler cultivates a large online following
that is able to carry out his mission even

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.600
in the event of his capture.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.770
He does this by releasing videos of himself
committing crimes and declaring his vengeance

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.899
on the corrupt rulers of the city.

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:31.619
This vengeance plays out in full when the
Riddler is incarcerated in Arkham State Hospital.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:36.070
When he's interrogated by Batman, he reveals
that he has placed car bombs throughout Gotham

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.070
City.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:41.450
The bombs go off, destroying Gotham's breakwater
walls, which causes considerable damage when

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.950
the city is flooded.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.650
This upheaval is all part of the Riddler's
scheme: The chaos acts as a distraction, enabling

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:52.079
his cult-like followers to carry out the assassination
of mayor-elect Bella Reál.

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:56.799
However, with the help of Catwoman, Batman
is able to take down the Riddler's "fans"

00:01:56.799 --> 00:01:59.539
and prevent the assassination from taking
place.

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:02.929
It's not enough that the Riddler enacts a
large number of heinous acts throughout the

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:08.179
film — he also films them and releases the
footage to "inspire" Gotham City's wayward

00:02:08.179 --> 00:02:09.179
minds.

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:13.739
This elevates the Riddler from a common criminal
into a genuine monster.

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:18.489
As mob boss Carmine Falcone's crimes against
the city are exposed, Catwoman vows to kill

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:21.620
Falcone — who is also her estranged father.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.409
She takes off for the Iceberg Lounge with
Batman and Gordon following closely behind.

00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:30.850
Once she gets into Falcone's office, Catwoman
points a gun at him — but before she can

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.700
fire a fatal shot, Batman stops her.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.010
He turns Falcone over to Gordon and the Gotham
City Police Department.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.980
After he's read his rights, the Penguin pulls
out a gun and prepares to kill Falcone himself.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.980
But then Falcone is shot dead by the Riddler
instead, who's ensconced in a nearby building.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.980
Falcone is no angel, having committed plenty
of crimes all over Gotham City over the course

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.260
of decades.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.120
But this is but one of many murders the Riddler
commits throughout the course of the film.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.080
Given that it's simply a kill with a gun actually
makes it one of the tamest.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.500
The worst are yet to come…

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:10.357
"I'm just here to unmask the truth about this
cesspool we call a city."

00:03:10.357 --> 00:03:14.250
At the point in time "The Batman" takes place,
James Gordon has not yet risen to the rank

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:18.140
of police commissioner, the role he's most
associated with as a character.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:22.220
Instead, the commissioner of the Gotham City
Police Department is Pete Savage.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:27.659
In stark contrast to Gordon's steadfast morality,
Savage is deeply corrupt, having accepted

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:29.989
bribes from various criminals.

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:34.099
Shortly after Mayor Don Mitchell Jr. is killed
by the Riddler, Commissioner Savage holds

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:35.170
a press conference.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:40.200
He announces the terrible news and promises
to bring the Riddler to justice for his crime.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.760
However, before he can carry out this vow,
he's killed by the Riddler.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.030
The villain leaves a message for Batman and
releases a disturbing video of Savage's death

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.030
to the public.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:53.430
What makes this kill so disturbing is how
Riddler does it — by trapping Savage's head

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.260
in a twisted maze with some hungry rats.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:01.630
Distributing the footage of the killing makes
this an especially cold-blooded crime.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:07.240
District Attorney Gil Colson is another respected-yet-crooked
member of Gotham City's elite: Batman discovers

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:10.489
early on that he's working for crime boss
Carmine Falcone.

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:14.340
However, this doesn't make his death at the
Riddler's hands any less appalling.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:18.970
During a funeral service for the late Mayor
Don Mitchell Jr., a car careens into the church

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.870
where everyone is gathered.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:25.310
Out comes Colson, who has a phone attached
to his hand and a bomb attached to his neck.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:29.330
Bruce Wayne, who is attending the funeral,
leaves, then returns as Batman to talk to

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.680
the Riddler via the phone in Colson's hand.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.840
The Riddler threatens to set off the bomb
unless Colson can correctly answer his three

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:36.840
riddles.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:40.669
With Batman's help, Colson manages to answer
the first two — but he can't bring himself

00:04:40.669 --> 00:04:44.590
to answer the third, which would reveal the
informant who helped the Gotham City Police

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:48.250
Department bring down crime boss Salvatore
Maroni.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:52.669
The Riddler proceeds to detonate the bomb,
killing Colson, and sending Batman flying

00:04:52.669 --> 00:04:53.669
backward.

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:54.840
So, let's recap.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:58.810
The Riddler ruins the funeral service for
the mayor he killed, kidnaps and torments

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:02.020
the district attorney, and then horrifically
murders him.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:07.690
As if that's not bad enough, he also broadcasts
the event live to his growing online audience.

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:12.580
The Riddler's worst moment is also his first:
Brutally killing the mayor of Gotham City,

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.940
Don Mitchell Jr., on Halloween night.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.470
It's a brazen way to kick off his vicious
campaign, and he couldn't have done it in

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:20.440
a more cold-blooded way.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:24.671
Shortly after watching news coverage of Mitchell's
mayoral debate with Bella Reál, the Riddler

00:05:24.671 --> 00:05:27.710
sneaks into his home and viciously beats him
to death.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:31.470
He leaves Mitchell's body propped up on a
chair with his head wrapped in duct tape,

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:34.360
with the words "NO MORE LIES" scrawled across
his face.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:38.180
To add to the gruesomeness of this crime,
Mitchell's thumb is removed and later found

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:43.330
attached to a USB drive in his car, giving
new meaning to the phrase "thumb drive."

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:47.190
The drive contains photos of Mitchell with
another woman, revealing that he was having

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:48.190
an affair.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:52.950
When Batman and Gordon plug the drive in,
it automatically leaks the photos to the media.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:57.419
He kills the man, and then completely obliterates
his legacy — and, as you may recall, his

00:05:57.419 --> 00:05:59.220
funeral — after the fact.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:03.360
Thanks to the Riddler's cruelty, Mitchell's
wife and child don't just lose him — they

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.120
lose their good memories of him too.

